From: Luke Howard <lukeh@padl.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bootstrap: build SwiftPM with the native build system

swift-bootstrap defaults to BuildSystemProvider.Kind.swiftbuild in 6.4
(Sources/swift-bootstrap/main.swift). When Utilities/bootstrap uses the
freshly built swift-bootstrap to rebuild SwiftPM, that engine deadlocks
partway through planning:

    [Pre-planning 1 / 4371]
    [Planning 1 / 4371]
    *** Could not create wakeup socket pair for CFSocket!!!
    [Planning 3264 / 4371]
    <hangs indefinitely, machine idle>

CoreFoundation fails to create its runloop wakeup socket pair, so the
notification that a child process exited never arrives. swift-bootstrap
sits in sigsuspend() with clang children left as zombies and never makes
further progress. It is not resource exhaustion -- the process had 31 open
descriptors against a 1048576 limit.

The legacy "native" engine does not exhibit this. It is deprecated in 6.4
but still present and selectable, and is already what meta-swift uses for
cross-compiling target Swift packages.

There is no less invasive way to select it: swift-bootstrap reads no
environment variable for this, Utilities/bootstrap does not pass
--build-system in its bootstrap branch, and swift's swiftpm.py product
only forwards additional_params to Utilities/bootstrap, which does not
relay unknown arguments onward.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [workaround for an upstream bug, not yet reported]
---
 Utilities/bootstrap | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/Utilities/bootstrap
+++ b/Utilities/bootstrap
@@ -728,6 +728,10 @@ def get_swiftpm_build_args(args):
     if args.bootstrap:
         swiftpm_args.append("SWIFTPM_CUSTOM_LIBS_DIR=" + os.path.join(args.bootstrap_dir, "pm"))
         swiftpm_args.append(os.path.join(args.bootstrap_dir, "bin/swift-bootstrap"))
+        # swift-bootstrap defaults to the swiftbuild engine in 6.4, which
+        # deadlocks during planning (CFSocket wakeup socket pair failure ->
+        # child-exit notifications never arrive). Use the legacy engine.
+        swiftpm_args += ["--build-system", "native"]
     else:
         swiftpm_args.append(args.swift_build_path or os.path.join(os.path.split(args.swiftc_path)[0], "swift-build"))
         swiftpm_args.append("--disable-sandbox")
